      "writtenOn": "2024-07-25T18:21:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t quite true since most UPSTREAM-tagged patches come from mainline, not from stable kernels.\n\nIf this patch were cherry-picked from the stable branch (`v6.1.96`), then we\u0027d see `commit ecf848eb934b03959918f5269f64c0e52bc23998 upstream.` in the commit message - which we don\u0027t. The commit should be the one that was actually used.\n\nHaving said that, I agree that it would preferred to actually cherry-pick the patch from the stable kernel - in which case it should be cited in this comment (and the actual upstream sha1 would be in the commit message) - but this is an uncommon case since LTS is merged into the ACK branch monthly or bi-monthly.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
